# AI-Powered ABSA MLOps Platform

This project is a production-inspired AI/MLOps platform for Vietnamese Aspect-Based Sentiment Analysis (ABSA) running on AWS with a serverless-first architecture.

### PROJECT GOALS

The system must support:
- AI inference
- dataset auditing
- analytics dashboard
- retraining pipeline
- monitoring
- CI/CD
- Infrastructure as Code
- model versioning
- production-inspired deployment

This project is:
- cloud-native
- serverless-first
- MLOps-oriented
- event-driven
- portfolio-quality
- graduation thesis quality

### TECH STACK

Frontend:
- Next.js App Router
- TypeScript
- TailwindCSS
- shadcn/ui
- Recharts
- Framer Motion

Backend:
- Python
- FastAPI-style architecture
- AWS Lambda

Cloud:
- AWS API Gateway
- AWS Lambda
- AWS SageMaker
- AWS Step Functions
- Amazon S3
- PostgreSQL RDS
- CloudWatch
- Route53
- ACM

Infrastructure:
- Terraform
- GitHub Actions

AI/ML:
- PyTorch
- Transformers
- ViBERTa
- CRF decoding
- Multi-task learning

### ARCHITECTURE RULES

Important:
- Prefer serverless AWS services
- Avoid overengineering
- Do NOT use Kubernetes/EKS
- Do NOT use Kafka
- Keep architecture realistic and deployable by a single engineer
- Focus on maintainability and demoability
- Use modular architecture
- Use production-inspired folder structures

### FRONTEND RULES

Frontend style:
- Modern SaaS dashboard
- shadcn admin dashboard style
- Clean enterprise UI
- Dark mode support
- Responsive design
- Dashboard-oriented layout

Frontend sections:
- Prediction page
- Analytics dashboard
- Admin dashboard
- Monitoring dashboard

Use:
- reusable components
- modular structure
- clean Tailwind styling
- loading skeletons
- charts for analytics

Follow installed skills:
- vercel-react-best-practices
- frontend-design
- web-design-guidelines

Frontend expectations:
- Use clean spacing and layout hierarchy
- Use reusable shadcn/ui components
- Use enterprise SaaS dashboard patterns
- Prefer composable React components
- Keep pages modular and scalable
- Prioritize UX clarity and responsive behavior

### BACKEND RULES

Backend must:
- use modular architecture
- separate business logic
- use service layers
- keep Lambda handlers lightweight
- support scalability
- follow clean API design

Backend structure expectations:
- routes/
- services/
- models/
- utils/
- schemas/
- config/

Prefer:
- dependency injection patterns
- reusable utilities
- structured logging
- environment-based configuration

### MLOPS RULES

The platform must support:
- dataset auditing
- model versioning
- retraining pipeline
- inference logging
- monitoring
- drift observation
- evaluation pipeline

MLOps principles:
- reproducibility
- modular pipelines
- maintainable workflows
- production-inspired lifecycle

### TERRAFORM RULES

Terraform structure:
- modular
- reusable
- environment-based
- production-inspired

Modules:
- lambda
- api_gateway
- s3
- iam
- sagemaker
- step_functions
- cloudwatch
- route53
- acm

Terraform expectations:
- separate environments
- reusable variables
- outputs
- clean module boundaries
- scalable infrastructure layout

### CI/CD RULES

GitHub Actions should support:
- frontend deployment
- lambda deployment
- terraform validation
- terraform plan/apply
- automated testing

CI/CD expectations:
- reusable workflows
- clean deployment stages
- environment separation
- scalable automation structure

### REPOSITORY STRUCTURE

```text
absa-mlops-platform/
│
├── frontend/
├── backend/
├── lambda/
├── training/
├── model/
├── infrastructure/
